{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the Canaanite was then in the land.</b> Rashi explained that he was going and conquering from the seed of Shem, for the land fell to Shem's portion when Noah divided the land among his sons. And it is puzzling, for in the parashat shelach lekha Rashi explained on the verse ״וחברון שבע שנים נבנתה״ that Mitzrayim gave it to his firstborn son, but it was built from everything good, like one of the seven of Tzoan, and so it is concluded in Sotah, chapter ואלו נאמרין — thus it implies that Hebron, which is in the land of Israel, fell to the portion of Ham. One may answer that it is a dispute, for in Torat Kohanim it concludes: for what reason did the Canaanites merit to dwell in their land 47 years more than the Egyptians? How? Seven years that Hebron was built before Tzoan of Egypt, and forty years that Israel dwelt in the wilderness after Egypt was destroyed — because they set aside a portion for Abraham the righteous and said to him: ״נשיא אלהים אתה בתוכנו״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The text of the Torat Kohanim derivation is hyper-literal; the logical flow of the 47-year calculation (7 + 40) is preserved as written without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:22.132105454Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}